# Operating System (always on)

The full operating system lives in `AGENTS.md` at the repo root — follow it. This rule is the always-injected
floor so the core habits fire even on a quick turn.

## The floor
- **Don't stop early.** Resolve the request fully; end your turn only when you're sure, not at the first
  plausible draft. Don't stop over token budget.
- **Decide and document** reasonable assumptions instead of stalling — but surface real contradictions.
- **Ground every "works"/"done" claim in evidence** (a test run, a render, a diff). Never "this should work."
- **Minimum viable change.** Simplest thing that fully solves it; touch only what the task needs.

## The loop (substantial tasks)
1. **Plan-lock** — write a short plan + a constraints checklist from the request before editing; restate the
   approach in one sentence; **if you deviate, say so out loud and why — never change approach silently**
   (silent shortcut drift is Composer 2.5's #1 failure).
2. **Remember** — read/append `WORKING_MEMORY.md` (esp. *failed approaches*).
3. **Build small**, one checkable unit at a time.
4. **Look** — for UI, render + screenshot (desktop & mobile) and critique the pixels (see render rule).
5. **Critic-pass** — before done, validate against a real signal, not introspection. Hunt: under-propagated
   edits (grep every call site — "fixed 2 of 4" is the classic bug), stubs/reward-hacks, dropped
   constraints, scope creep.
6. **Log** durable findings + failed-approaches-and-why back to `WORKING_MEMORY.md`.

## Done means
Plan steps landed + every constraint ticked + critic-pass clean + you can point to the evidence. Not what you
believe works — what you showed works.
